    "text": "Let the tangent to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math> at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> meet the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and normal at it meet the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi></math> at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>. Then the area (in sq. units) of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to:",
